    "result_text": "All 7 tests pass. The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI moved date-derived values onto a **fiscal-year basis** (fiscal year starts 1 July, named by the calendar year it ends in \u2014 the Australian convention, e.g. 1 July 2026\u201330 June 2027 = `FY27`).\n\n**New unit \u2014 `util/FiscalYear.java`** (single responsibility: fiscal-year math on a `LocalDate`):\n- `of(date)` \u2014 the fiscal year (its ending calendar year); the date's own year before 1 July, next year on/after.\n- `label(date)` \u2014 `'FY<YY>'`.\n- `elapsed(from, to)` \u2014 whole fiscal years crossed between two dates.\n\n**`OwnerMapper`** \u2014 reuses `FiscalYear`:\n- `membershipNumber` year segment now uses `FiscalYear.of(registrationDate) % 100` instead of the calendar year (`M27` for today's Sept-2026 date, previously `M26`).\n- Added a `fiscalYear(owner)` deriver + `@Mapping`, returning `FiscalYear.label(registrationDate)` (null when the date is absent).\n\n**`AssignOwnerMembershipPoints`** \u2014 tenure now counts **elapsed fiscal years** via `FiscalYear.elapsed(...)` (`> 1` fiscal year) rather than a 365-day window; dropped the now-unused `ChronoUnit` import and renamed the constant/helper accordingly. A newly-registered owner still has zero tenure, so never earns the bonus.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `fiscalYear` (`FY<YY>`) field to `OwnerDto` (so the generated DTO gets the setter MapStruct needs) and updated the `membershipNumber`/`membershipPoints` descriptions. Touched the `ApplyOwnerRegistrationDate` javadoc for accuracy.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreReturnsFiscalYear` passes (`fiscalYear` matches `FY\\d{2}`), and the existing `BusinessDayTest` (6) remains green \u2014 7/7 overall.\n\nNote on the naming convention: `FY<YY>` is named by the year the fiscal year *ends* (dominant AU business convention, matching the app's AU theming). The acceptance test only checks the `FY\\d{2}` format, so it doesn't pin the convention \u2014 flag this if your spec intends naming by the *start* year instead, which is a one-line change in `FiscalYear.of`.",
